{"tool_name":"dithering","contents":["neubias"],"fetched_metadata":{"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"markdown","processed":"","summary":"","value":"Dithering is a type of half tone thresholding where greyscale (or RGB channel) intensity is converted into a local density of binary pixels. This is ideal for rendering images in devices with a binary output such as printers (greyscale) or with a small number of colours (colour dithering). \r\nThe following methods have been implemented (there are several more): \r\n\r\n- Floyd-Steinberg\r\n- Atkinson\r\n- Jarvis-Judice-Ninke\r\n- Stucki\r\n- Bayer_2x2\r\n- Bayer_4x4\r\n- Bayer_8x8\r\n- Clustered_4x4\r\n- Random\r\n\r\n[Here is a good text explaining various dithering algorithm. ](http://www.tannerhelland.com/4660/dithering-eleven-algorithms-source-code/)"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2019-01-10T14:00:50+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2013-10-11T13:08:43+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[],"comments_2023":[],"free_tagging":[],"give_feedback_on_this_soft":[{"cid":0,"comment_count":0,"last_comment_name":null,"last_comment_timestamp":1505206713,"last_comment_uid":164,"status":2}],"has_author":[{"value":"Gabriel Landini"}],"has_biological_terms":[],"has_comparison":[],"has_documentation":[{"options":[],"title":"","uri":"https://imagej.net/Dithering"}],"has_doi":[],"has_entry_curator":[{"target_id":94,"target_type":"user","target_uuid":"aa749c9e-5b9a-4fdf-83ce-6b94538fe57c","url":"/user/94"}],"has_function":[{"target_id":4063,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3434","url":"/conversion"}],"has_implementation":[],"has_interaction_level":[{"target_id":3574,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"a22a3a50-0fbb-41ee-944a-38e0b86ac077","url":"/taxonomy/term/3574"}],"has_license":[],"has_location":[{"options":[],"title":"","uri":"https://imagej.net/Dithering"}],"has_programming_language":[{"target_id":359